    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>Ogres are greedy raiders and hulking gluttons born of hateful supernatural forces. From gloomy ruins and desolate wilds, they raid defenseless communities and ambush travelers. Ogres crave food and treasure, and they take spiteful pleasure in smashing art, books, clockwork and anything else delicate or lovingly made. Sometimes they carry off victims to eat later or, more rarely, performers who catch their fancy. Ogres trace their origins to wrathful gods such as Erythnul, Takhisis and Vaprak, and they rise magically from the earth of lands corrupted by evil deities, dark magic or ancient curses. Some bear the marks of the place that spawned them, such as rocky calluses, mossy growths or frostbitten scars.</p><p>Ogrillons are Humanoids transformed by foul magic or by the will of a wrathful god. They still look like who they once were, but they grow over 8 feet tall and take on ogre-like features. Supernatural rage boils inside them constantly; some struggle to hold it back, others deliberately unleash it on other creatures.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
